ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football SP+ rankings for all 138 FBS teams","description":"The updated SP+ rankings, plus strength of schedule and résumé SP+, after this weekend's results.","published":"2026-11-22T15:10:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49868647/2026-college-football-sp+-rankings-all-138-fbs-teams","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Utah extends longest active winning streak in FBS, clinches Big 12 title bid","description":"Devon Dampier threw a 68-yard touchdown pass before halftime and an 85-yard clincher in the fourth quarter as No. 2 Utah beat TCU 38-17 for its 17th straight victory, clinching a spot in the Big 12 championship game.","published":"2026-11-22T13:27:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50561074/no-2-utah-seals-spot-big-12-title-game-beating-tcu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Boise State's 4th-down gamble backfires as upset loss deals blow to CFP hopes","description":"Boise State's decision to go for it on fourth down instead of punting ended up backfiring when San Diego State got the stop and went on to kick a game-winning 42-yard field goal Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-22T07:46:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50560141/boise-state-4th-gamble-backfires-san-diego-state-wins","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chaos takes over the Big Ten: UCLA, Indiana and Ohio State all lose in Week 12","description":"UCLA, Indiana and Ohio State all lost to unranked teams in a year where parity is the ever-present theme.","published":"2026-11-22T07:25:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedayfinal112126/week-12-top-games-highlights-takeaways","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Predicting the College Football Playoff: Who's most likely to make the field?","description":"Find out which teams our experts think will make this season's CFP.","published":"2026-11-22T06:30:41.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/playoffpredictions112126/cfp-predictions-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"College Football Playoff top 12 projection after Week 12","description":"We assess how the selection committee could stack the top teams in the country after Week 12.","published":"2026-11-22T14:49:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50552244/projecting-2026-playoff-top-12-week-12-cfp","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-22T05:08:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's jab at Ohio State's 'THE' leads top Week 12 CFB trolls","description":"Nebraska deployed a simple but effective troll that poked fun at its opponent's propensity to emphasize the \"the\" in \"The Ohio State University.\"","published":"2026-11-22T04:22:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50554531/nebraska-ohio-state-trolls-college-football-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4871005/teitum-tuioti","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teitum_Tuioti"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Teitum Tuioti","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teitum_Tuioti","description":"American football linebacker","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:42Z","intro":"Teitum Tuioti is an American college football linebacker for the Oregon Ducks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Tuioti attended Lincoln Southeast High School in Lincoln, Nebraska for three years before transferring to Sheldon High School in Eugene, Oregon, ahead of his senior season. He was rated as a three star recruit and committed to play college football for the Oregon Ducks over offers from schools such as Nebraska, Kansas State, Texas Tech, Oregon State, California, Washington and Boise State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In week 4 of the 2023 season, Tuioti recorded his first career sack in a win over Colorado. He finished his first collegiate season in 2023 with 30 tackles with four being for a loss, and two sacks. In the Ducks' 2024 spring game, Tuioti notched five tackles and two and a half sacks. That season, he appeared in 14 games, where he totaled 58 tackles with eight being for a loss, five and a half sacks, a pass deflection, and a forced fumble for Oregon."}]}}